      <item>
       <widget class="QLabel" name="label">
        <property name="text">
         <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:696; font-style:italic; color:#285471;&quot;&gt;QuESt Planning&lt;/span&gt; tool, developed by Sandia National Laboratories, is a long-term capacity expansion planning model that examines the role of energy storage technologies on optimal generation and transmission expansion. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:696; font-style:italic; color:#285471;&quot;&gt;Key features include:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px; -qt-list-indent: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;Identification of cost-optimal energy storage, generation, and transmission investments&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;Sizing and siting of energy storage resources &amp;amp; generation &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;Scenario-based planning and model flexibility&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Segoe UI'; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;To run advanced simulations, proceed to the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/sandialabs/quest_planning&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Segoe UI'; font-style:italic; text-decoration: underline; color:#0000ff;&quot;&gt;QuESt Planning GitHub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Segoe UI'; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;page for further instructions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;Acknowledgement&lt;/span&gt;: This material is based upon work supported by the U.S. Department of Energy, Office of Electricity (OE), Energy Storage Division.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
        </property>
